arm_gic: the GICv2 aliased CPU interface registers (AIAR, AEOIR, AHPPIR)

A GICv2 with the Security Extensions has Secure-only aliases of the
Non-secure IAR, EOIR and HPPIR at GICC + 0x20 / 0x24 / 0x28 (GICv2
architecture spec, 4.4.13 - 4.4.15): Secure software reads 0x20 to take a
Group 1 interrupt as the Non-secure side would.  The model logged "Bad
offset" and read zero.

Rockchip's vendor kernels with CONFIG_FIQ_GLUE (RV1103 / RV1106 / RV1126
SDKs, for the FIQ debugger) run Linux in the Secure state, put every
interrupt in Group 1 and take them from GICC_AIAR in gic_handle_irq():
reading 0 there is interrupt 0 forever, and the boot hangs right after
"Starting kernel".  Implement the three aliases for Secure accesses on a
GIC with groups; they stay RAZ/WI for Non-secure accesses and on GICs
without the Security Extensions.

---
diff --git a/hw/intc/arm_gic.c b/hw/intc/arm_gic.c
index 899f133..703742d 100644
--- a/hw/intc/arm_gic.c
+++ b/hw/intc/arm_gic.c
@@ -1662,6 +1662,24 @@ static MemTxResult gic_cpu_read(GICState *s, int cpu, int offset,
             *data = s->abpr[cpu];
         }
         break;
+    case 0x20: /* Aliased Interrupt Acknowledge */
+    case 0x28: /* Aliased Highest Priority Pending Interrupt */
+        /*
+         * GICv2 with security extensions: a Secure access sees the
+         * Non-secure (Group 1) IAR / HPPIR.  Non-secure accesses and GICs
+         * without groups: RAZ.
+         */
+        if (s->revision != 2 || !gic_has_groups(s) ||
+            gic_cpu_ns_access(s, cpu, attrs) || gic_is_vcpu(cpu)) {
+            *data = 0;
+        } else {
+            MemTxAttrs ns = attrs;
+
+            ns.secure = 0;
+            *data = offset == 0x20 ? gic_acknowledge_irq(s, cpu, ns)
+                                   : gic_get_current_pending_irq(s, cpu, ns);
+        }
+        break;
     case 0xd0: case 0xd4: case 0xd8: case 0xdc:
     {
         int regno = (offset - 0xd0) / 4;
@@ -1741,6 +1759,16 @@ static MemTxResult gic_cpu_write(GICState *s, int cpu, int offset,
     case 0x10: /* End Of Interrupt */
         gic_complete_irq(s, cpu, value & 0x3ff, attrs);
         return MEMTX_OK;
+    case 0x24: /* Aliased End Of Interrupt */
+        /* Secure access: the Non-secure EOIR (see Aliased Acknowledge) */
+        if (s->revision == 2 && gic_has_groups(s) &&
+            !gic_cpu_ns_access(s, cpu, attrs) && !gic_is_vcpu(cpu)) {
+            MemTxAttrs ns = attrs;
+
+            ns.secure = 0;
+            gic_complete_irq(s, cpu, value & 0x3ff, ns);
+        }
+        return MEMTX_OK;
     case 0x1c: /* Aliased Binary Point */
         if (!gic_has_groups(s) || (gic_cpu_ns_access(s, cpu, attrs))) {
             /* unimplemented, or NS access: RAZ/WI */
